// Title: Conhost.exe CommandLine Path Traversal
// Sigma ID: ee5e119b-1f75-4b34-add8-3be976961e39
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-06-14 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059.003
// Description: detects the usage of path traversal in conhost.exe indicating possible command/argument
//   confusion/hijacking
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://pentestlab.blog/2020/07/06/indirect-command-execution/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_conhost_path_traversal.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessCommandLine contains "conhost" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/../../"
